            <ArticleTitle>[Clinical characteristics of acute pancreatitis in Mexico].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>167-73</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.rgmx.2012.08.002</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0375-0906(12)00112-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Acute pancreatitis (AP) etiology and frequency vary in relation to geographic region.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="AIMS" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To determine the etiology, frequency, and mortality of AP in a Mexican population.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="PATIENTS AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">We carried out a prospective study of first episode AP patients over a period of 6 years.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">A total of 605 patients with a mean age of 40 years were included in the study. Sixty-four percent of them presented with overweight and/or obesity determined through BMI. Etiology was biliary in 66.60%, it was due to alcohol consumption in 15.90%, hypertriglyceridemia in 7.80%, it was post-endoscopic retrograde cholangiopancreatography (ERCP) in 2.10%, and was undetermined in 7.20%. Pancreatic infection was suspected in 70 patients and they underwent CT-guided fine needle aspiration. Thirty-two of those patients were diagnosed with pancreatic infection in which Staphylococcus spp was the most common microorganism. Overall mortality was 5.00% (2.60% &lt; 30 years and 10.00% &gt; 70 years). Necrosis, pancreatic infection, and mortality were more frequent in the cases in which etiology was due to alcohol ingestion.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The most frequent AP etiology was biliary, but that caused by alcohol presented with more complications. Overall mortality was 5.00% and was higher in the elderly patients.</AbstractText>
